00:23:30.190 --> 00:23:31.350
That's a good way to put it.

551
00:23:31.410 --> 00:23:33.150
He has some maturing to do.

552
00:23:33.290 --> 00:23:34.430
So anyway, he freaks out.

553
00:23:34.550 --> 00:23:37.050
He wants to turn off the lights and have everyone hide.

554
00:23:37.290 --> 00:23:39.830
But do you remember how we couldn't get it coordinated, Jenna?

555
00:23:39.970 --> 00:23:42.910
Like we couldn't turn off the lights at the right time.

556
00:23:43.170 --> 00:23:43.570
Yes.

557
00:23:43.730 --> 00:23:48.190
People should know that in this scene, when Michael runs over to shut off the light switches,

558
00:23:48.190 --> 00:23:51.510
those light switches do not actually operate the lights.

559
00:23:51.790 --> 00:23:56.630
The lights are controlled by a grid and a guy who's in charge of them.

560
00:23:57.310 --> 00:24:03.350
And so what they would do is they would have someone on a radio who would see when Steve

561
00:24:03.350 --> 00:24:06.510
hit the light switch, and then they would radio go.

562
00:24:06.770 --> 00:24:11.150
And then the light switch guy would actually turn off the lights.

563
00:24:11.410 --> 00:24:13.910
But it didn't always work.

564
00:24:13.910 --> 00:24:17.490
So sometimes Steve would hit the switch, and the lights would just stay on.

565
00:24:17.650 --> 00:24:22.550
Or sometimes they would anticipate too quickly, and the lights would go off before he hit the

566
00:24:22.550 --> 00:24:22.950
switch.

567
00:24:23.270 --> 00:24:26.590
Again, this is one of those moments where I'm like, thank God we didn't have to do any car

568
00:24:26.590 --> 00:24:27.770
chases or explosions.

569
00:24:28.110 --> 00:24:29.030
It's so true.

570
00:24:29.270 --> 00:24:31.870
It seems like the light switch was really tricky for us.

571
00:24:31.970 --> 00:24:33.630
I have to ask you one thing.

572
00:24:33.790 --> 00:24:36.990
OK, so Sadiq from IT is coming to help Michael, right?

573
00:24:36.990 --> 00:24:44.850
I just have to say this, Jenna, at 1 minute 26 seconds, this actually, like, I thought about

574
00:24:44.850 --> 00:24:48.630
this for days after watching this episode.

575
00:24:49.210 --> 00:24:54.410
Michael says he tried to install the software himself, but it was password protected.

576
00:24:55.030 --> 00:24:58.010
Sadiq says that just means you have to enter your password.

577
00:24:58.870 --> 00:25:03.750
Does this mean that Sadiq didn't even have to come there?

578
00:25:03.750 --> 00:25:10.250
If Michael had just entered 1234 that was on the Post-it note, had he just entered that,

579
00:25:10.370 --> 00:25:11.350
the software would have installed?

580
00:25:12.390 --> 00:25:13.910
I think that's what that means.

581
00:25:14.070 --> 00:25:19.310
So that is so, like, if you put that in perspective, Sadiq is probably like, this idiot.

582
00:25:19.870 --> 00:25:26.070
All he had to do was enter the password I put on a Post-it note and taped to his desktop.

583
00:25:26.570 --> 00:25:30.070
It also feels like something that could have been solved with a phone call.

584
00:25:30.370 --> 00:25:30.810
Yes.

585
00:25:31.250 --> 00:25:31.690
Yes.

586
00:25:31.690 --> 00:25:36.970
He definitely did not need to come into the office and be subjected to Michael's cold open.

587
00:25:37.170 --> 00:25:37.610
No, no.

588
00:25:38.070 --> 00:25:39.130
Oh, my gosh.

589
00:25:39.350 --> 00:25:46.410
So at 1 minute 46 seconds, Dwight surprises Michael outside of his office, right?

590
00:25:46.530 --> 00:25:49.050
He's demanding to know why the IT guy is there.

591
00:25:49.150 --> 00:25:52.610
And of course, Michael doesn't want to tell him because it's going to be revealed that

592
00:25:52.610 --> 00:25:56.850
