I think Pam was just as excited that Roy couldn't attend as Jim is.

1005
00:42:23.720 --> 00:42:26.000
Yeah, I think Roy probably has some dude hangout.

1006
00:42:26.200 --> 00:42:28.300
He's very—he's kind of a dude dude, right?

1007
00:42:28.840 --> 00:42:29.220
Yeah.

1008
00:42:29.220 --> 00:42:31.840
He probably has his thing, and also, Roy—

1009
00:42:31.840 --> 00:42:32.720
Roy wouldn't want to go.

1010
00:42:32.820 --> 00:42:37.040
I was going to say, the last thing Roy wants to do is hang out with any of the Dunder Mifflin

1011
00:42:37.040 --> 00:42:38.640
employees who's sort of over it.

1012
00:42:38.700 --> 00:42:40.700
They have to do enough of that probably for him.

1013
00:42:41.020 --> 00:42:46.120
So he was, I think, happy to sit this one out, and Pam was like, oh, my God, oh, my God,

1014
00:42:46.180 --> 00:42:46.560
oh, my God.

1015
00:42:46.600 --> 00:42:47.600
And so was Jim.

1016
00:42:47.600 --> 00:42:53.380
I'm, like, totally making this up, but maybe Pam waited kind of till the last minute to

1017
00:42:53.380 --> 00:42:57.140
tell Roy about the party so that it would be less likely that he could attend.

1018
00:42:57.320 --> 00:43:00.160
Like, I could see her maybe doing that.

1019
00:43:00.340 --> 00:43:03.220
And I could see her downplaying it, like, ugh, you know, I don't know.

1020
00:43:03.300 --> 00:43:04.220
It's the thing I have to go to.

1021
00:43:04.420 --> 00:43:05.060
Everyone's going.

1022
00:43:06.240 --> 00:43:06.880
Yes, 100%.

1023
00:43:07.260 --> 00:43:08.200
It's going to be lame.

1024
00:43:08.320 --> 00:43:08.780
You know what?

1025
00:43:08.780 --> 00:43:09.980
If you don't want to go, you don't have to.

1026
00:43:10.140 --> 00:43:10.740
Yeah, it's fine.

1027
00:43:10.740 --> 00:43:15.420
I'll go because I feel like I have to, but I don't want you to have to change your plans.

1028
00:43:15.540 --> 00:43:16.120
I totally get it.

1029
00:43:16.180 --> 00:43:17.200
If you don't want to go, it's okay.

1030
00:43:17.600 --> 00:43:19.660
That's 100% how that went down, I believe.

1031
00:43:20.040 --> 00:43:20.440
Yes.

1032
00:43:21.120 --> 00:43:21.460
All right.

1033
00:43:21.600 --> 00:43:25.940
So now everyone's trying to get out of the office, and they're trying to avoid Michael

1034
00:43:25.940 --> 00:43:28.540
because they all know he's not invited.

1035
00:43:28.700 --> 00:43:32.700
So people are making up excuses to not hang out with him that night.

1036
00:43:33.000 --> 00:43:34.680
And Angela, you have a great one.

1037
00:43:34.940 --> 00:43:37.840
You say, charity, bake, drive.

1038
00:43:38.440 --> 00:43:39.020
Oh, yeah.

1039
00:43:39.100 --> 00:43:39.380
I'm sure.

1040
00:43:39.460 --> 00:43:41.080
My character's, like, horrible at lying.

1041
00:43:41.200 --> 00:43:41.560
Horrible.

1042
00:43:41.800 --> 00:43:45.640
Well, a lot of people wrote in to ask if our excuses were scripted or improvised.

1043
00:43:45.640 --> 00:43:47.960
Angela, was yours scripted or improvised?

1044
00:43:48.120 --> 00:43:49.020
Mine is a combo.

1045
00:43:49.300 --> 00:43:52.480
So my scripted line was charity, bake, drive.

1046
00:43:52.680 --> 00:43:54.800
And then Michael's scripted line was liar.

1047
00:43:55.180 --> 00:43:59.200
And then Steve improvised, you are a liar.

1048
00:43:59.420 --> 00:44:02.620
And then I improvised, no, I'm not, as I left.

1049
00:44:03.260 --> 00:44:04.860
And I didn't even look back.

1050
00:44:05.060 --> 00:44:06.120
And it stayed in.

1051
00:44:06.200 --> 00:44:09.800
And I think it's great because that's exactly how my character, I think, would have responded.

1052
00:44:09.980 --> 00:44:10.260
Yes.

1053
00:44:10.420 --> 00:44:13.680
I just love that Dwight says he has soccer and clarinet practice.

1054
00:44:14.480 --> 00:44:14.900
Yes.

1055
00:44:15.340 --> 00:44:16.180
And you know what?

1056
00:44:16.240 --> 00:44:19.440
I feel like sometimes, I mean, you know, we have young children.

1057
00:44:19.440 --> 00:44:24.500
And sometimes when they're bad at lying, they just sort of list what their activities are.

1058
00:44:24.500 --> 00:44:31.840
So I sort of feel like Dwight probably growing up had clarinet and soccer practice and he just went to default.

1059
00:44:32.260 --> 00:44:37.220
Also, as Dwight leaves, he says, see you Monday, Michael.

1060
00:44:37.600 --> 00:44:40.220
Casual Friday tracker coming at you.

1061
00:44:40.360 --> 00:44:41.500
No one's dressed casual.

1062
00:44:41.800 --> 00:44:42.180
No.

1063
00:44:42.400 --> 00:44:45.000
It's clearly a Friday because he says, see you Monday.

1064
00:44:45.700 --> 00:44:49.820
None of us are dressed casually, even though we're going to a barbecue after work.

1065
00:44:50.000 --> 00:44:51.760
Well, people are going to change clothes.

1066
00:44:52.000 --> 00:44:53.700
Don't you think they're going to go home and freshen up?

1067
00:44:53.700 --> 00:44:54.360
I don't want to.

1068
00:44:54.540 --> 00:44:57.060
Listen, it's still not casual Friday.

1069
00:44:57.320 --> 00:44:57.980
I get it.

1070
00:44:58.080 --> 00:44:58.480
I get it.

1071
00:44:58.660 --> 00:45:01.920
We still set up in a previous episode that we have casual Fridays.

1072
00:45:02.160 --> 00:45:04.920
And yet here it is, a Friday, and none of us are dressed casually.

1073
00:45:05.020 --> 00:45:05.580
No, you're right.

1074
00:45:05.660 --> 00:45:06.040
You're right.

1075
00:45:06.040 --> 00:45:07.180
I'm going to stay on this.

1076
00:45:07.280 --> 00:45:08.480
I think you stay on it.

1077
00:45:08.480 --> 00:45:09.280
Don't worry, everybody.

1078
00:45:09.600 --> 00:45:10.720
I'm on it.

1079
00:45:11.120 --> 00:45:12.320
I'm on the mail cart.

1080
00:45:12.880 --> 00:45:14.220
I'm on casual Friday.

1081
00:45:14.500 --> 00:45:16.860
And we will continue to track Mindy's hair.

1082
00:45:17.320 --> 00:45:18.980
Don't anyone lose sleep over it.

1083
00:45:19.040 --> 00:45:19.560
We're on it.

1084
00:45:19.720 --> 00:45:22.380
Oh, I'm, as you know, obsessed with Mindy's hair.

1085
00:45:22.520 --> 00:45:23.020
I'm obsessed.

1086
00:45:23.020 --> 00:45:25.940
I have one thing to say before we go to the party.

1087
00:45:26.220 --> 00:45:26.560
Yeah.

1088
00:45:27.120 --> 00:45:31.020
And again, this was like the Sadiq moment in the cold open for me.

1089
00:45:31.180 --> 00:45:33.160
It's something I thought probably way too much about.

1090
00:45:34.120 --> 00:45:37.480
Wouldn't Jim have known that Michael saw the Evite?

1091
00:45:38.540 --> 00:45:41.520
This is the day he gets access to everyone's emails.

1092
00:45:42.420 --> 00:45:45.220
Jim clearly sent it to everyone's work email.

1093
00:45:45.620 --> 00:45:45.800
Yeah.

1094
00:45:46.140 --> 00:45:47.140
Wouldn't he have known?

1095
00:45:47.140 --> 00:45:49.020
He knows Michael knows, right?

1096
00:45:49.880 --> 00:45:53.140
Well, he knows Michael knows, by the way, Michael is behaving.

1097
00:45:53.440 --> 00:45:59.120
But you're saying as soon as he got access to the emails, the first thought Jim would have

1098
00:45:59.120 --> 00:46:00.560
would be, oh, no.

1099
00:46:00.800 --> 00:46:01.740
The Evite's there.

1100
00:46:01.900 --> 00:46:03.800
The Evite's sitting in everyone's email.

1101
00:46:03.940 --> 00:46:04.720
He's going to know.

1102
00:46:04.720 --> 00:46:12.320
Well, similarly, how did we get all the way to the day of the party before Dwight thinks

1103
00:46:12.320 --> 00:46:13.700
to mention the party to Michael?

1104
00:46:13.840 --> 00:46:18.660
There's that scene where Dwight starts bringing up the party and Jim shushes him.

1105
00:46:18.720 --> 00:46:19.820
He's like, no, no, no.

1106
00:46:19.900 --> 00:46:20.600
Don't say anything.

1107
00:46:21.340 --> 00:46:23.740
You're telling me, I mean, when did he send out the Evite?

1108
00:46:23.960 --> 00:46:25.220
At least a week ago.

1109
00:46:25.920 --> 00:46:31.040
In that whole week, he didn't have to, like, keep the shush on Dwight?

1110
00:46:31.180 --> 00:46:35.000
No, that didn't bump me as much because I feel like, I don't know.

1111
00:46:35.160 --> 00:46:39.100
I know, I feel like, listen, guys, this isn't all dudes.

1112
00:46:39.560 --> 00:46:43.180
But I know from my experience with fellas, they probably aren't going to think about the

1113
00:46:43.180 --> 00:46:44.080
party till the day of.

1114
00:46:44.440 --> 00:46:48.300
You know, they're not like, it's not like Dwight is, like, thinking about this party every

1115
00:46:48.300 --> 00:46:48.520
day.

1116
00:46:48.680 --> 00:46:50.260
He's got, you know, he's busy.

1117
00:46:50.260 --> 00:46:51.040
He's busy.

1118
00:46:51.240 --> 00:46:52.920
He's managing a secret relationship with Angela.

1119
00:46:53.100 --> 00:46:55.640
Yeah, he's tracking yeast infections in Scranton.

1120
00:46:55.880 --> 00:46:57.080
Yeah, he's got a lot going on.

1121
00:46:57.260 --> 00:46:57.920
He's got a lot going on.

1122
00:46:58.040 --> 00:46:58.780
All right, fair enough.

1123
00:46:59.220 --> 00:47:00.760
All right, guys, we're going to take a break.

1124
00:47:00.760 --> 00:47:04.620
And when we come back, we're going to a party, a barbecue at Jim's house.

1125
00:47:04.820 --> 00:47:05.900
We're going to tell you all about it.

1126
00:47:12.420 --> 00:47:13.000
Are you ready?

1127
00:47:13.080 --> 00:47:13.900
You want to lay those out?

1128
00:47:15.300 --> 00:47:16.180
Do you want to lay them out?

1129
00:47:16.400 --> 00:47:17.440
I don't want to rush you.

1130
00:47:17.560 --> 00:47:18.300
She's back.

1131
00:47:18.820 --> 00:47:21.420
She got some food and the sass is back.

1132
00:47:21.560 --> 00:47:25.960
You guys, before we went to break, Jenna was getting a little lightheaded because she was

1133
00:47:25.960 --> 00:47:26.720
really hungry.

1134
00:47:26.920 --> 00:47:27.180
Yeah.

1135
00:47:27.340 --> 00:47:31.880
So if you notice a tonal shift in this last part of the podcast, it's because we took

1136
00:47:31.880 --> 00:47:35.580
an actual break during our break and we ate a full lunch.

1137
00:47:35.720 --> 00:47:36.080
We ate.

1138
00:47:36.160 --> 00:47:37.340
Jenna and I eat lunch together.

1139
00:47:37.340 --> 00:47:41.020
And it kind of reminds me of how we had lunch every day on the set at The Office.

1140
00:47:41.100 --> 00:47:41.500
I know.

1141
00:47:41.820 --> 00:47:43.320
I love it so much.

1142
00:47:43.340 --> 00:47:47.340
I was just talking to Lee last night where I said, well, he asked me a question.

1143
00:47:47.460 --> 00:47:48.820
He was watching the episode with me.

1144
00:47:48.860 --> 00:47:52.000
And he said, what's it like for you to watch these episodes again?

1145
00:47:52.740 --> 00:47:53.840
Does it bring you back?

1146
00:47:54.080 --> 00:48:00.680
And I said, it really, the flood of memories that come back to me and the most prevalent

1147
00:48:00.680 --> 00:48:03.340
is how much we laughed together as a caSt.

1148
00:48:03.820 --> 00:48:09.640
And I said, and now I do this podcast with Angela and we laugh the same way when we do

1149
00:48:09.640 --> 00:48:13.460
the podcast and when we edit the podcast and we eat lunch the same way.

1150
00:48:13.600 --> 00:48:16.920
And now I'm tearing up because we just had one of our lunches.

1151
00:48:17.140 --> 00:48:17.320
Yeah.

1152
00:48:17.520 --> 00:48:19.460
That lunch in particular, Jenna, was a good one.

1153
00:48:19.520 --> 00:48:20.180
It was a good one.

1154
00:48:20.260 --> 00:48:24.440
And it really reminded me, we navigated nine years of our lives.

1155
00:48:24.440 --> 00:48:29.520
A lot happened to both of us and we shared a lot at lunch.

1156
00:48:29.700 --> 00:48:31.820
And some days it was just little tiny things.

1157
00:48:31.960 --> 00:48:33.800
And then some days we had huge heart-to-hearts.

1158
00:48:34.020 --> 00:48:36.540
And Jenna and I just now had a really pretty big heart-to-heart.

1159
00:48:36.740 --> 00:48:41.420
Those lunches were like, sometimes they're like a therapy session.

1160
00:48:41.580 --> 00:48:44.060
They're better than a therapy session because it's your BFF.

1161
00:48:44.080 --> 00:48:44.980
It's your BFF.

1162
00:48:45.400 --> 00:48:46.060
That's right.

1163
00:48:46.220 --> 00:48:46.660
All right.

1164
00:48:46.740 --> 00:48:47.660
We're back, guys.

1165
00:48:47.820 --> 00:48:48.700
We're full of food.

1166
00:48:48.900 --> 00:48:49.220
Okay.

1167
00:48:49.700 --> 00:48:51.720
And I'm going to start with a fan question.

1168
00:48:52.020 --> 00:48:52.460
Do it.

1169
00:48:52.460 --> 00:48:53.220
How about that?

1170
00:48:53.340 --> 00:48:54.480
From Rob Fish.

1171
00:48:54.900 --> 00:48:55.140
Okay.

1172
00:48:55.240 --> 00:48:58.300
He says, whose house was used for Jim's barbecue?

1173
00:48:58.660 --> 00:48:59.320
Because that's right.

1174
00:48:59.480 --> 00:49:01.340
We're go to this barbecue at Jim's house.

1175
00:49:01.500 --> 00:49:05.120
So for the house, we shot in a real neighborhood in Northern California.

1176
00:49:05.140 --> 00:49:06.480
It wasn't a set.

1177
00:49:06.800 --> 00:49:11.380
And we had to have really unusual shooting hours because it was a night shoot.

1178
00:49:11.460 --> 00:49:14.560
And there was really nighttime outside of the windows.

1179
00:49:14.800 --> 00:49:17.120
So we usually would shoot from like 6 a.m.

1180
00:49:17.180 --> 00:49:17.900
to 6 p.m.

1181
00:49:17.960 --> 00:49:19.420
when we were shooting at Dunder Mifflin.

1182
00:49:19.700 --> 00:49:22.220
But here we were really shooting more in the evening.

1183
00:49:22.460 --> 00:49:26.560
Now, if they were shooting into the house, it didn't matter what was outside.

1184
00:49:26.560 --> 00:49:27.800
They could black out the windows.

1185
00:49:27.820 --> 00:49:30.240
But for all those shots outside, it was really night.

1186
00:49:30.380 --> 00:49:33.000
And some nights, we stayed past 10 p.m.

1187
00:49:33.200 --> 00:49:33.880
And do you remember?

1188
00:49:33.920 --> 00:49:34.980
We'd get a little bit tired.

1189
00:49:35.340 --> 00:49:35.520
Yeah.

1190
00:49:35.520 --> 00:49:37.380
We'd get a little loopy as of 9 p.m.

1191
00:49:37.640 --> 00:49:43.500
And this was the first time where we shot offset, like really offset since the Dundies.

1192
00:49:43.820 --> 00:49:46.120
And we always had a lot of fun when we would do that.

1193
00:49:46.360 --> 00:49:46.560
Yeah.

1194
00:49:46.560 --> 00:49:51.860
And also, I remember there wasn't really like a place between scenes for you to go.

1195
00:49:52.260 --> 00:49:52.500
No.

1196
00:49:52.640 --> 00:49:54.740
And I don't remember our trailers being there.

1197
00:49:54.880 --> 00:49:55.100
No.

1198
00:49:55.200 --> 00:49:57.320
I think they couldn't park them in the neighborhood.

1199
00:49:57.320 --> 00:49:58.140
They were far away.

1200
00:49:58.140 --> 00:49:59.680
So they would shuttle us in.

1201
00:49:59.900 --> 00:50:02.900
And so in between scenes, we just really all hung out.

1202
00:50:02.980 --> 00:50:03.400
Kind of.

1203
00:50:03.400 --> 00:50:04.980
In that little living room, kind of.

1204
00:50:05.080 --> 00:50:05.480
Totally.

1205
00:50:05.780 --> 00:50:08.380
This leads me to a fan question by Rufio.

1206
00:50:08.380 --> 00:50:12.680
He said, when you had to go to the bathroom, did you use the actual bathroom in the house?

1207
00:50:12.680 --> 00:50:13.880
Or did you go offset?

1208
00:50:14.560 --> 00:50:15.680
I don't remember.

1209
00:50:15.960 --> 00:50:21.220
But I, because a lot of times you shoot in houses and they'll tape the toilet closed and

1210
00:50:21.220 --> 00:50:22.240
put a little sign on it.

1211
00:50:22.340 --> 00:50:23.980
And it says, do not use.

1212
00:50:24.240 --> 00:50:25.540
And you have to go outside.

1213
00:50:25.680 --> 00:50:28.340
They have like those porta potty things outside.

1214
00:50:28.700 --> 00:50:32.960
Or they'll rent the house next door and that becomes a holding area for everyone.

1215
00:50:33.240 --> 00:50:35.020
And maybe you can pee in the holding house.

1216
00:50:35.240 --> 00:50:37.700
I peed in John and Jim's house.

1217
00:50:37.700 --> 00:50:38.760
Oh, no.

1218
00:50:39.160 --> 00:50:41.420
Well, I don't remember the toilet being taped shut.

1219
00:50:41.880 --> 00:50:44.440
I remember them saying that I could go.

1220
00:50:44.640 --> 00:50:48.880
And I, like, you know, quickly, I used, there was like a hall bathroom or something.

1221
00:50:49.140 --> 00:50:52.860
Well, sometimes they would let cast members use the bathrooms in the house.

1222
00:50:53.040 --> 00:50:55.940
But then they would have porta potties for the crew, which I always thought was kind

1223
00:50:55.940 --> 00:50:56.460
of lousy.

1224
00:50:56.660 --> 00:51:00.540
Well, I know one time it was explained to me by an AD because I was like, well, wait,

1225
00:51:00.680 --> 00:51:01.900
where's the bathroom everyone's using?

1226
00:51:02.120 --> 00:51:07.360
And she said to me that they could not afford for us to go too far away.

1227
00:51:07.780 --> 00:51:08.900
Oh, that makes sense.

1228
00:51:09.020 --> 00:51:12.280
And so they often would have a bathroom for the actors a little bit closer.

1229
00:51:12.520 --> 00:51:12.700
Yeah.

1230
00:51:12.820 --> 00:51:14.500
Just purely because of timing.

1231
00:51:14.960 --> 00:51:15.100
Yeah.

1232
00:51:15.260 --> 00:51:17.880
So just know that so that you don't feel as bad.

1233
00:51:17.880 --> 00:51:18.720
So don't feel so guilty.

1234
00:51:18.920 --> 00:51:19.060
Yeah.

1235
00:51:19.260 --> 00:51:19.820
But it's true.

1236
00:51:19.900 --> 00:51:23.960
Like you said, our actual trailers were probably a 15-minute van ride away.

1237
00:51:24.200 --> 00:51:27.700
So they had to create a way for us to go to the bathroom that was a little closer

1238
00:51:27.700 --> 00:51:28.180
to the set.

1239
00:51:29.020 --> 00:51:29.660
All right.

1240
00:51:29.920 --> 00:51:34.160
So when we all get to the party, Jim takes everyone on a tour of his house.

1241
00:51:34.600 --> 00:51:36.260
Before we go on the tour.

1242
00:51:36.400 --> 00:51:36.960
Tell me.

1243
00:51:37.340 --> 00:51:39.760
There is something that I just love little things like this.

1244
00:51:39.880 --> 00:51:42.280
Did you notice everyone's party attire?

1245
00:51:42.420 --> 00:51:42.680
Wait.

1246
00:51:42.880 --> 00:51:43.480
I, yes.

1247
00:51:43.620 --> 00:51:44.860
I have that here too.

1248
00:51:45.280 --> 00:51:47.700
Can we talk about everyone's casual clothes?

1249
00:51:47.920 --> 00:51:48.280
Yes.

1250
