We are making sure to maximize this party for, like, maximum next-to-each-other time.

1753
01:12:10.020 --> 01:12:11.100
You're sitting next to each other.

1754
01:12:11.220 --> 01:12:16.160
The other thing I noticed throughout the party is that Jim's roommate and his girlfriend are all over each other.

1755
01:12:16.340 --> 01:12:17.460
They're constantly making out.

1756
01:12:17.580 --> 01:12:22.260
They're making out, or she's sitting on his lap, or she has a leg, like, over his leg.

1757
01:12:22.400 --> 01:12:26.320
And to say, those two people did not know each other before they started filming.

1758
01:12:26.940 --> 01:12:29.760
And, I mean, what is that job?

1759
01:12:29.760 --> 01:12:35.460
How do you get – I mean, I would feel so shy if I was – that was my job.

1760
01:12:35.660 --> 01:12:37.500
I was like, hi, nice to meet you.

1761
01:12:37.620 --> 01:12:40.760
I guess we're just going to hang on to each other all day.

1762
01:12:41.000 --> 01:12:42.900
For tonight while we shoot this thing.

1763
01:12:43.300 --> 01:12:44.080
Back to the scene.

1764
01:12:45.000 --> 01:12:48.900
Steve and John, as Jim and Michael, are harmonizing islands in the stream.

1765
01:12:48.900 --> 01:13:00.820
And then in the background, we go over their shoulder, and we slowly push in on Angela's feet and Dwight's feet bumping the Birkenstocks.

1766
01:13:00.940 --> 01:13:01.320
All right.

1767
01:13:01.440 --> 01:13:03.120
Let's break down this scene for a second.

1768
01:13:03.120 --> 01:13:04.700
I have to tell you some behind the scenes.

1769
01:13:04.900 --> 01:13:05.120
Okay.

1770
01:13:05.120 --> 01:13:07.100
I have some fan questions as well.

1771
01:13:07.180 --> 01:13:07.900
Well, ask them.

1772
01:13:08.020 --> 01:13:09.280
Perhaps they'll lead you in.

1773
01:13:09.320 --> 01:13:10.660
Maybe they're part of my note cards.

1774
01:13:10.800 --> 01:13:12.380
Well, this is not a fan question.

1775
01:13:12.380 --> 01:13:13.380
This is a me question.

1776
01:13:13.440 --> 01:13:14.640
What are you in?

1777
01:13:14.840 --> 01:13:15.780
Is it a shed?

1778
01:13:16.000 --> 01:13:17.140
Is it a doghouse?

1779
01:13:17.140 --> 01:13:20.080
It seems too small to be a shed and too large to be a doghouse.

1780
01:13:20.200 --> 01:13:20.820
What is it?

1781
01:13:20.960 --> 01:13:25.180
It looked like a giant dollhouse that people would buy for their little girl.

1782
01:13:25.380 --> 01:13:28.740
There was like a ramp of steps that went up to it.

1783
01:13:28.840 --> 01:13:29.060
Okay.

1784
01:13:29.080 --> 01:13:33.180
It looked like someone had bought this for their little girl to play in.

1785
01:13:33.500 --> 01:13:34.800
Like a fancy dollhouse.

1786
01:13:34.960 --> 01:13:35.120
Yeah.

1787
01:13:35.340 --> 01:13:37.620
Well, Angela, I have a fan question now.

1788
01:13:38.180 --> 01:13:42.160
A-Town and Nat Attack and Brooklyn Jade all want to know,

1789
01:13:42.760 --> 01:13:45.280
was that really Rain and Angela making out,

1790
01:13:45.280 --> 01:13:48.000
or were they just random stunt people wearing the same shoes?

1791
01:13:48.260 --> 01:13:51.120
And if it was them, did they talk?

1792
01:13:51.120 --> 01:13:52.620
How did they make it not weird?

1793
01:13:52.980 --> 01:13:53.760
I mean, yeah.

1794
01:13:53.860 --> 01:13:55.180
I think we all just want to know.

1795
01:13:55.220 --> 01:13:55.580
Okay.

1796
01:13:55.580 --> 01:13:56.780
How did that go down?

1797
01:13:56.960 --> 01:13:57.200
All right.

1798
01:13:57.300 --> 01:13:57.460
Okay.

1799
01:13:57.620 --> 01:13:59.280
So, of course, it's weird.

1800
01:13:59.440 --> 01:14:00.160
It's totally weird.

1801
01:14:00.340 --> 01:14:01.660
It was Rain and I.

1802
01:14:02.000 --> 01:14:03.260
We did not kiss, guys.

1803
01:14:03.380 --> 01:14:04.120
We did not make out.

1804
01:14:04.220 --> 01:14:06.260
In fact, it was really cold out in that dollhouse.

1805
01:14:06.360 --> 01:14:08.120
So, I had on a big, thick coat.

1806
01:14:08.280 --> 01:14:09.560
I had hand warmers.

1807
01:14:09.560 --> 01:14:13.500
But they did want to see our Birkenstocks a-bumpin'.

1808
01:14:13.500 --> 01:14:16.740
It was a little tricky because we had to time it out perfectly.

1809
01:14:17.000 --> 01:14:19.480
And we tried different positions of our feet.

1810
01:14:19.860 --> 01:14:20.700
Here's the thing.

1811
01:14:21.160 --> 01:14:23.020
Rainn Wilson is 6'3".

1812
01:14:23.020 --> 01:14:24.800
I am 5'1".

1813
01:14:24.800 --> 01:14:28.180
So, my feet did not hang out of the dollhouse.

1814
01:14:28.240 --> 01:14:28.980
Oh, my gosh.

1815
01:14:29.520 --> 01:14:29.920
Yeah.

1816
01:14:29.920 --> 01:14:34.540
If your bodies were positioned so that you could actually be kissing one another,

1817
01:14:34.760 --> 01:14:35.900
we would never see your feet.

1818
01:14:36.100 --> 01:14:36.440
No.

1819
01:14:36.840 --> 01:14:37.240
No.

1820
01:14:37.240 --> 01:14:41.480
So, we tried our feet in a few different positions so the camera could see them both.

1821
01:14:41.660 --> 01:14:44.000
We were laying side-by-side, kind of flipping our feet back and forth.

1822
01:14:44.140 --> 01:14:44.300
Okay.

1823
01:14:44.500 --> 01:14:49.800
And Paul Feig was like, you guys kind of look like you're doing a sad breaststroke swim or

1824
01:14:49.800 --> 01:14:50.080
something.

1825
01:14:50.400 --> 01:14:51.860
He was like, I don't know what you're doing.

1826
01:14:51.980 --> 01:14:52.880
It looks like you're swimming.

1827
01:14:53.520 --> 01:14:54.740
So, he was like, all right.

1828
01:14:54.820 --> 01:14:55.780
How do I say this?

1829
01:14:55.780 --> 01:14:57.140
This is somewhat awkward, Angela.

1830
01:14:57.380 --> 01:15:02.960
But I think you need to lay on your back and straddle Rainn.

1831
01:15:03.180 --> 01:15:03.380
Oh.

1832
01:15:03.380 --> 01:15:04.480
I was like, what?

1833
01:15:04.780 --> 01:15:05.680
And he said, yeah.

1834
01:15:05.680 --> 01:15:12.940
He said, I'd love to see your little feet wrap around his calves and rub back and forth.

1835
01:15:13.520 --> 01:15:20.580
So, in order for me to do this, you guys, my face was in his chest for you to see my feet.

1836
01:15:20.720 --> 01:15:21.960
Were you like suffocating?

1837
01:15:22.140 --> 01:15:22.560
Kind of.

1838
01:15:22.660 --> 01:15:23.200
I'm imagining.

1839
01:15:23.200 --> 01:15:24.400
Like, how are you breathing?

1840
01:15:24.760 --> 01:15:28.460
Rainn was also doing sort of like this painful kind of plank move.

1841
01:15:28.660 --> 01:15:30.120
So, he didn't crush you?

1842
01:15:30.200 --> 01:15:32.220
So, he didn't crush me so I could breathe.

1843
01:15:32.440 --> 01:15:37.300
And then I was like, how do I wrap my feet around his calf?

1844
01:15:37.500 --> 01:15:38.540
It's kind of awkward.

1845
01:15:38.680 --> 01:15:39.300
You know why?

1846
01:15:39.300 --> 01:15:40.560
Your ankles don't bend that way.

1847
01:15:40.560 --> 01:15:42.400
Your shins don't bend that way.

1848
01:15:42.400 --> 01:15:47.780
So, I was doing this weird, on action, Rainn would roll over on top of me, do his weird

1849
01:15:47.780 --> 01:15:48.680
plank move.

1850
01:15:48.980 --> 01:15:52.200
Like, in one take, it kind of took a long time and he started to shake a little.

1851
01:15:52.260 --> 01:15:52.600
Oh, dear.

1852
01:15:52.960 --> 01:15:58.240
All I will say is, Rainn, you're a very strong guy, but planking for him does take a toll

1853
01:15:58.240 --> 01:15:58.720
on people.

1854
01:15:58.980 --> 01:15:59.620
Take after take.

1855
01:15:59.740 --> 01:16:00.640
We did a bunch of takes.

1856
01:16:00.640 --> 01:16:00.840
Yeah.

1857
01:16:00.840 --> 01:16:04.320
And also, my feet were like in this weird position.

1858
01:16:04.500 --> 01:16:05.860
So, we did this every take.

1859
01:16:05.980 --> 01:16:09.720
And in between takes, we would roll on our backs side by side.

1860
01:16:09.880 --> 01:16:12.500
We would have these really deep conversations.

1861
01:16:13.360 --> 01:16:17.960
It was just one of those surreal moments where we were doing the most ridiculously silly thing.

1862
01:16:18.060 --> 01:16:21.140
And then in between, we talked about like our lives.

1863
01:16:21.140 --> 01:16:25.000
I feel like this is the moment where I really became friends with Rainn because we talked

1864
01:16:25.000 --> 01:16:30.140
about where we grew up and our childhoods and like what we believed in and just really

1865
01:16:30.140 --> 01:16:36.500
had this really huge heart-to-heart in between this plank straddle foot rubbing of the calf.

1866
01:16:36.680 --> 01:16:39.240
I did write about this in my journal as well.

1867
01:16:39.380 --> 01:16:39.720
Okay.

1868
01:16:39.880 --> 01:16:43.200
And I just said that I was really glad they weren't rolling sound out there.

1869
01:16:43.320 --> 01:16:47.660
We weren't miked because I was giggling so much whenever we had to rub feet.

1870
01:16:50.150 --> 01:16:50.630
Aw.

1871
01:16:51.230 --> 01:16:53.770
So, that kind of is the end of the episode.

1872
01:16:54.010 --> 01:16:54.750
That ends the episode.

1873
01:16:54.850 --> 01:16:59.010
There's a little tag where we go back to the improv class.

1874
01:16:59.010 --> 01:17:00.550
It's a little bit of a flashback.

1875
01:17:00.550 --> 01:17:05.570
I think that they just loved this monologue, this talking head that Steve gives so much

1876
01:17:05.570 --> 01:17:07.790
that they had to include it at the end of the episode.

1877
01:17:08.370 --> 01:17:11.210
But I don't know if you remember this, Angela.

1878
01:17:11.410 --> 01:17:14.590
That last night when we shot, we stayed till after midnight.

1879
01:17:14.910 --> 01:17:16.430
It was a really late night.

1880
01:17:16.650 --> 01:17:18.930
And I also wrote this in my journal.

1881
01:17:19.330 --> 01:17:23.530
I said, Steve ordered pizzas for the cast and crew.

1882
01:17:23.530 --> 01:17:29.610
And we all had a little bitty, kind of, I guess, mini party after the party.

1883
01:17:29.770 --> 01:17:31.250
He ordered Baroni's pizza.

1884
01:17:31.250 --> 01:17:32.230
Yeah, his favorite.

1885
01:17:32.350 --> 01:17:32.670
His favorite.

1886
01:17:32.750 --> 01:17:33.530
It was so good.

1887
01:17:33.670 --> 01:17:35.510
And that was really cool.

1888
01:17:35.690 --> 01:17:37.090
I love that we kept journals.

1889
01:17:37.690 --> 01:17:39.570
Women in our 30s journaling.

1890
01:17:40.870 --> 01:17:42.770
We were 80 when we were 30.

1891
01:17:43.270 --> 01:17:45.610
We're almost to our appropriate age.

1892
01:17:45.610 --> 01:17:46.370
I think so.

1893
01:17:46.750 --> 01:17:47.330
All right, guys.

1894
01:17:47.550 --> 01:17:48.530
Thank you so much.

1895
01:17:48.690 --> 01:17:50.070
We cannot wait.

1896
01:17:50.430 --> 01:17:52.970
Next week is the Christmas episode.

1897
01:17:53.150 --> 01:17:54.950
The first Christmas episode.

1898
01:17:55.070 --> 01:17:56.150
And we have a lot to say.

1899
01:17:56.610 --> 01:17:57.310
Yankee Swap.

1900
01:17:57.990 --> 01:17:59.510
Thank you so much, Ken Jeong.

1901
01:17:59.830 --> 01:18:01.270
Joel McHale, not so much.

1902
01:18:02.030 --> 01:18:03.610
And we'll see you next week.

1903
01:18:04.590 --> 01:18:06.610
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.

1904
